Summary in W's Framework:

What – Start converting lambda_execution_role from two regional roles into one shared role.

What for – Satisfy the requirement that East and West use the existing global IAM role.

How – Remove the regional suffix from IAM role naming → East creates the role → West looks it up → expose a common local.lambda_execution_role_arn → consumers use that local.

Where – Start in main.tf and iam.tf; then update Lambda files and kms.tf.

When – Do this before deleting the existing -w2 role, and don't apply yet because the IAM policy still needs consolidation.

Who – East Terraform owns the shared role; West Terraform consumes it; Lambdas and KMS in both regions reference it.

Why – IAM roles are global → a separate West execution role is unnecessary → but West still needs an execution-role ARN → therefore West should reference the shared role rather than create another one → both regions can then authorize the same role against their regional resources.

